  "details": "# Issue:\n\nWhen \"Clearing All\" nodes of the camera dolly you sometimes are left with the actual cameras still being there.\n\nThis happens when having a least 2 paths, using multi stream and having let the path play at least once. Then pressing clear will remove all nodes and the camera on the first path, but all the other cameras will still stay there.\n\nThose \"ghost\" cameras don't seem to actually be rendering anything, but they are still visible to other players as well and even persist between world switches. (Though when switching worlds they appear to only be visible to the local user)\n\n**Reproduction Steps:**\n\n1. Open the Camera and Switch to the dolly section\n\n2. Create the first path with e.g. 3 nodes\n\n3. Create a second path with e.g. 3 nodes\n\n4. Switch the Streaming Mode to \"Multi\"\n\n5. Play the dolly animation\n\n6. Let the animation finish and then press \"Clear All\"\n\nFor more detailed info on my used camera settings view the attachments below.\n\n# Expected Behaviour:\n\nAll cameras and nodes should be deleted when pressing \"Clear All\".\n\n# Attachments:\n\nHere is a video of me reproducing the issue:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/qFd8QYxW8Dw\n\nHere are a few screenshots showcasing the issue as well as my camera settings:",
